task: default-retable
agent: opus5-bench
started: 2026-09-08
branch: feature/default-retable
worktree: ../okay-wt-retable

why: `Channel.apply`'s default changed from a plain ring to `growing`
  (17404a4e). Every table whose lanes reach a channel through that
  default now describes a tree nobody has — the same stale-number
  problem this session has been correcting all day, except this time I
  caused it.

what: re-measure the classes that go through the DEFAULT and rewrite
  their tables. Surveyed rather than guessed:
    through the default   MergeBenchmark, ScalingBenchmark,
                          ChunkFlushBenchmark, IdiomaticApiBenchmark
    explicit mechanisms   ChannelGranularity, ChannelGuarantee,
                          ManyProducers, Adversarial — these build
                          AbruptChannel / SentinelChannel / StmChannel
                          or a Queues builder by name and do NOT move
  So four classes are re-run and four are not, and the ones that are
  not get checked rather than assumed: a control lane from each is
  compared against its recorded value.

predict: `Source.merge` and the ChunkFlush merges improve — the sweep
  already showed `Source.merge` 20% ahead at capacity 256 and 1024 and
  level at 64. The Idiomatic channel lanes should be flat, since they
  run ONE producer, where growing never grows.
  DISQUALIFYING: if a lane that should not have moved has moved, the
  survey above is wrong and I re-run everything rather than publish a
  table built on a wrong list.
